                <pb facs="0632" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.00 Nazi/68</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Luther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-20">February 20, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In pursuance to our
                    conversation of yesterday and in compliance with your request I beg to give you
                    the information concerning the membership of members of the National Socialist
                    Party in the Association of the “Friends of the New Germany” as follows:</p>
                <p>The Foreign Department of the National Socialist Party has, according to this
                    information, definitely forbidden its members to belong to the “Association of
                    the Friends of the New Germany” (Bund der Freunde des Neuen Deutschland), which
                    is not an organization recognized by the Party. Each member of the Party
                    residing in the United States will receive by mail a circular letter containing
                    the request to immediately notify the Foreign Department of the National
                    Socialist Party of his resignation from the Association of the Friends of the
                    New Germany. The circular letter emphasizes furthermore that there is no branch
                    of the National Socialist Party in existence in the United States and that
                    members of the party are strictly forbidden to make propaganda among
                    Non-Germans.</p>
                <p>With my highest consideration [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Luther</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
